  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   - **Central Idea**: Use a projective coordinate descent algorithm that explicitly minimizes the overlap integral by leveraging gradient information from correlation calculations. This approach introduces a new adaptive distance metric for updating solutions and ensures global optimality at each grid size.\n   - **Bottleneck Addressed**: The previous algorithm relied solely on deterministic coordinate descent which accelerated convergence but stumbled into local optima. This method injects stochastic elements and uses gradient information to navigate the complex optimization landscape more effectively.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   - **Variables**: Represent h(x) as step function samples over [0,2] with sample count n_points and spacing dx=2.0/n_points.\n   - **Constraints**:\n     - Bounded values: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n     - Integral constraint: \u2211h[i] \u00b7 dx = 1\n   - **Objective**: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \u2248 max_k (max(corr)\u00b7dx) where corr is the full correlation with 1-h.\n   - **Smoothed Objective**: Use a novel smooth_max function based on the Laplace mechanism to maintain gradient information in the optimization process:\n     `smooth_max(corr, \u03b1) = max(correlation values) + \u03b2 \u00b7 exp(-\u03b3(|k|))` \n     where \u03b2 and \u03b3 incorporate lag-position weights and distance from mode to bound the correlation impact.\n   - **Formulation Insight**: The gradient is minimized using the adjoint of the correlation operator, updating each coordinate based on the negative gradient component.\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   - **Input Validation**: \n     - Check grid length of initial_h_values is even (n_points)\n     - Project initial_h_values to sum(\u00b7)=n_points/2 using project_to_sum\n   - **Grid Exploration**:\n     - Start at base grid n_base=160 (even)\n     - Double grid size until acceptable: n=320,640 (max size 640 within time)\n     - Use list of grid sizes: [160,320,640]\n   - **Coordinate Descent**:\n     - For each grid size:\n        1. Initialize random candidate (standard normal perturbation)\n        2. For each iteration:\n           a. Compute correlation: corr = correlate(h,1-h,'full')\n           b. Compute g = gradient of smooth_max w.r.t h (via adjoint method)\n           c. Compute update distance: d = abs(\u2207C\u2085) * current_grid_step (adaptive weight)\n           d. Apply update with normalized grad component\n           e. Compute new objective and refine if improvement\n        3. Maintain best candidate from each optimization\n   - **Adaptive Control**:\n     - Grid step size: quadratic decay from 1.0 to 0.1 with iterations\n     - Smoothness parameter \u03b1: starts at 50 for base grid, decays by 0.8 per doubling\n     - Stochastic update: every 4th iteration injects noise proportional to current grid size\n   - **Objective Computation**:\n     - `compute_c5(h, dx)` computes C\u2085 directly via correlation\n     - `smooth_max(corr, \u03b1)` softens the max operation for gradient descent\n     - `update_coordinate(i, dx, \u03b1)` adjusts single coordinate using Laplacian updates\n\n4. **Search Choices**\n   - **Grid Strategy**: Start coarse then increase to medium only to avoid excessive computation\n   - **Update Mechanism**: Uses adaptive projection with built-in correlation gradient checking\n   - **Optimization Controls**:\n     - Initial randomization weight: 0.25 (saturated by projection)\n     - Step decay: second-order adaptive decay with focus parameters [0.7, 0.8]\n     - Noise addition: Gaussian with \u03c3 = grid_size^0.3 (arcsinh-normalized)\n     - Objective monitoring: stop if improvement stalls after 100k function evals\n   - **Rationale**: Noise addition prevents local stagnation, gradient uses Laplace smoothing to approximate discontinuous derivatives\n\n5. **Compute Budget & Robustness**\n   - **Dominant Cost**: Grid halving (1/2) empirical scaling. Total estimates:\n     - Base grid (160): ~45s\n     - 320: ~120s\n     - 640: ~200s (total falling ~365s)\n   - **Fallback**: Coarse grid solution if time constraint hit\n   - **Termination checks**: \n     - Grid transition after 80% of budget passed\n     - Objective below 0.38 stops early\n     - Time constraint: 1300s limit strictly enforced\n   - **Validation**:\n     - Post-optimization ensure 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 with tolerance 1e-6\n     - Final objective computed with `compute_c5`\n\n6. **Validation & Return Contract**\n   - **Checks**:\n     - 0\u2264h_values[i]\u22641 for all i with torch 1e-6 absolute tolerance\n     - np.isfinite(c5_bound)\n     - np.abs(c5_bound - max_correlation*dx)\u22641e-8\n     - n_points must be even integer\n   - **Returns**:\n     - h_values: numpy array passed through project_to_sum\n     - c5_bound: float using compute_c5 with mode=\"full\"\n     - n_points: grid size used",
